# Mobile Performance

Target platform: **mobile devices** running Godot 2D viewer.

## Simulation Side

- Keep snapshot JSON compact; avoid redundant per-tick data.
- Batch entity updates; use stable entity IDs for diffing.
- Target tick budget: configurable, default 10–20 ticks/sec for economy-heavy scenarios.

## Godot Viewer Side

- Render from snapshot layers; avoid per-frame Python round-trips.
- Use sprite atlases and pooled nodes where possible.
- Optional hex grid overlay must be toggleable (hidden by default on mobile).
- Limit diagnostic overlay complexity on low-end devices.

## Snapshot Size Guidance

- Full map snapshot should stay under ~2 MB JSON for typical trial maps.
- Use layer culling and viewport-based interest management in later runs.

See `docs/design/06_mobile_2d_visual_design.md` for visual layer stack and UX budgets.
